{"head":44,"savepointDataFileId":"780521064771","savepointListObject":{"9":{"revisionId":9,"timestamp":1614281864694,"state":"saved","type":"session","diffAuthorList":{"248126054":true}},"39":{"revisionId":39,"timestamp":1614292674343,"state":"saved","type":"session","diffAuthorList":{"248126054":true}}},"lastEditTimestamp":1614343018677,"diffChangeset":"Z:15d>9q|f=12f=2v*4|1+1|1=1*4|1+1*4*8*e*6+c*4|1+1*4*2*a*3+1*4*e*6+v*4*e*6*i+t*4|1+1*4*2*j*3+1*4*e*6+f*4|1+1*4*2*j*3+1*4*e*6+1y*4|2+2*4*2*a*3+1*4*e*6+14*4*e*6*k+w*4|1+1*4*2*j*3+1*4*e*6+t*4|1+1*4*2*j*3+1*4*e*6+22*4|3+3$\n\nRELATED WORK\n*Alternate AML Data and Models: https://github.com/IBM/AMLSim\n*Focus on models\n*Data generation does not use detailed virtual world approach used here\n\n*Synthetic credit card transaction data: https://github.com/IBM/TabFormer\n*Labeled for fraud / not-fraud\n*Github site contains both data and Transformer-based fraud detection model\n\n\n","invalidDiffChangeset":false,"authorList":{"248126054":{"authorName":"Erik Altman","authorCustomAvatarUrl":"/users/248126054/avatar"}},"diffAuthorList":{"248126054":true},"shouldCreateSavepointBeforeApplyingNextRevision":false,"firstKeyRevision":5,"atext":{"text":"#############################################\nAdditional Documentation:  PDF Deck\n#############################################\n\nAML = Anti Money Laundering\n\nThis AML data is in CSV format and represents financial transactions -- bank transfers, purchases, credit card transactions, checks, etc. Most of the transactions are legitimate. A few represent money laundering. A laundering tag is provided with each transaction. With that laundering tag, AML models can use this data for training and to test their inferences.\n\nThe data is generated using a multi-agent virtual world model. All of the agents in the virtual world have actions governed by statistical distributions. Thus the model and data are NOT based on obfuscating or anonymizing real individuals. Everything is synthetic. More specifically the underlying model uses a virtual world of banks, individuals, and companies -- with individuals and companies buying items, and doing bank transfers to make payments, get supplies, pay salaries, etc. The underlying model has good and bad actors, with bad actors doing things like smuggling, extortion, illegal gambling, etc. The bad actors sometimes attempt to launder ill-gotten funds resulting in money-laundering transactions.\n\nData Characteristics\n\n*3000 Individuals\n*Transactions span 1 month:  January 2019\n*trans_3000p2_list.txt file lists all 45,351,509 transactions\n*Transactions are among entities (individuals, corporations, partnerships, etc) via their bank accounts\n\n\nRELATED WORK\n*Alternate AML Data and Models: https://github.com/IBM/AMLSim\n*Focus on models\n*Data generation does not use detailed virtual world approach used here\n\n*Synthetic credit card transaction data: https://github.com/IBM/TabFormer\n*Labeled for fraud / not-fraud\n*Github site contains both data and Transformer-based fraud detection model\n\n\n\n\n","attribs":"*4*5*6*7+19*4|1+1*4*5*6+r*4*8*5*6*d+8*4|1+1*4*6+19*4|2+2*4*8*e*6+3*4*e*6+3*4*8*e*6*g+1*4*e*6+4*4*8*e*6*g+1*4*e*6+5*4*8*e*6*g+1*4*e*6+9*4*6|2+2*4*e*6+5z*4*e*6*f+a*4*e*6+1e*4*e*6*f+a*4*e*6+25*4*6|2+2*4*e*6+jv*4|2+2*4*8*5*6+k*4|2+2*4*2*a*3+1*4*5*6+g*4|1+1*4*2*a*3+1*4*5*6+14*4|1+1*4*2*a*3+1*4*8*5*6+m*4*5*6+12*4|1+1*4*2*a*3+1*4*5*6+2u*4|3+3*4*8*e*6+c*4|1+1*4*2*a*3+1*4*e*6+v*4*e*6*i+t*4|1+1*4*2*j*3+1*4*e*6+f*4|1+1*4*2*j*3+1*4*e*6+1y*4|2+2*4*2*a*3+1*4*e*6+14*4*e*6*k+w*4|1+1*4*2*j*3+1*4*e*6+t*4|1+1*4*2*j*3+1*4*e*6+22*4|4+4|1+1","opCount":62,"appliedAttribsCount":175,"maxAttribsOnSingleOp":5},"pool":{"numToAttrib":{"0":["author","a.4fz9s4pIrvcRKF5l"],"1":["align","left"],"2":["insertorder","first"],"3":["lmkr","1"],"4":["author","248126054"],"5":["font-color-000000","true"],"6":["font-size-large","true"],"7":["font-size-medium","true"],"8":["bold","true"],"9":["link-MTYxNDI4MTY3OTE4MC1odHRwczovL2libS5lbnQuYm94LmNvbS9maWxlLzc2MDM5NjEyNTIyMQ==","true"],"10":["list","bullet1"],"11":["removed","true"],"12":["link-MTYxNDI4MTY3OTE4MC1odHRwczovL2libS5lbnQuYm94LmNvbS9maWxlLzc2MDM5NjEyNTIyMQ==",""],"13":["link-MTYxNDI4MTg2NjUyMy1odHRwczovL2libS5lbnQuYm94LmNvbS92L0FNTC1BbnRpLU1vbmV5LUxhdW5kZXJpbmctRGF0YS9maWxlLzc4MDUxNTA0NTcwNw==","true"],"14":["font-color-24292e","true"],"15":["italic","true"],"16":["underline","true"],"17":["font-size-medium",""],"18":["link-MTYxNDM0MzAxNTA1Ny1odHRwczovL2dpdGh1Yi5jb20vSUJNL0FNTFNpbQ==","true"],"19":["list","bullet2"],"20":["link-MTYxNDM0MzAxNTA2Ni1odHRwczovL2dpdGh1Yi5jb20vSUJNL1RhYkZvcm1lcg==","true"]},"nextNum":21},"chatHead":-1,"publicStatus":false,"passwordHash":null,"savedRevisions":[]}